WEBVTT

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.420
I'm a human. I was a human.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.750
Your species is tanuki, huh?

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.960
No! I'm a raccoon!

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.220
If you were a raccoon,
your tail would have stripes.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.720
You're a bona fide tanuki.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.180
I'm no tanuki!

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.350
Follow me.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.440
THESE SCUM ARE THE BARBARIC BOMBERS.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.070
It looks like he got here first again.

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.720
Hold on a second!
Where am I following you--

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.310
How long will you keep that tail out?

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.440
Switch back to your human form.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.900
Actually...

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.940
You can't?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.030
Right.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.990
I thought he'd be a lot older.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:07.710
What?

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.000
-What's wrong?
-Nobody is a beastman.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.340
Of course not.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.800
But until just now...

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.760
That was for the festival.
This is how we are normally.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.510
What? You're kidding!

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.600
About what?

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.520
I thought everyone was always
in their beast form here.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.100
Quit talking like a human.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.900
I told you. I am a human.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.410
BEASTMAN-COOPERATIVE

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.910
<i>This is the place.</i>

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.420
She's a beastman, all right.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.540
What? You can tell from that?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.130
The beastman marker test
is a simple yet reliable test.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.300
You are, without a doubt, a beastman.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.970
I am not! I'm a human!

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:09.430
I don't need to use the marker test to see
that you're clearly a beastman.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.520
I swear I'm a human!

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.020
I was an ordinary human a year ago.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.730
Then suddenly I turned into this.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.110
Impossible.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.780
Humans are humans. Beastmen are beastmen.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.410
It's been that way from the start.
Nobody changes.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.620
It must be a disease or something!

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.790
A disease?

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:32.080
Yes, a disease! A beastman disease!

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.580
There are other people like me
in this city, right?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.540
There's nobody like that.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.220
Well, I haven't heard of anyone like that.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:50.890
Recently, others have an odd disease
where they imagine they're humans.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.350
Why don't you see a doctor--

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.400
It's not that kind of disease!

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.270
Jem, don't say things like that.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:01.570
Show some sensitivity, would you?

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.860
I'm so sorry.
Your name is Kagemori, is it?

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.740
Yes. I'm Michiru Kagemori.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.120
I'm Melissa.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.000
He may not look it, but Jem here is
the Chairman of the Beastman-Cooperative.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.040
It's our job to look after any newcomers.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.090
You'll need to register
at the city hall tomorrow,

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.760
so fill this out.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.800
BEASTMAN RESIDENT REGISTRATION FORM

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:30.060
I told you! I'm really not a beastman!
I can't register as a beastman!

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.140
There's not much I can do about that.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.980
I know! My student ID!

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.480
"Student ID"?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:41.030
My student ID has my blood type
and species on it.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.570
Since humans and beastmen
have different blood types,

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.660
it will clear everything up,
so there are no mistakes...

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.700
It was stolen,

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.580
along with my wallet.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.790
Oh, dear. Then I guess
you'll just have to forget about it.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:58.790
You can't be serious!

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:03.510
Anything stolen in Anima-City
can never be retrieved.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.050
Why don't you get some sleep for now?

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.220
You look terribly exhausted.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.980
For today,
you'll have to put up with just this.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.310
The bed is clean though.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.020
It's plenty. I've been sleeping outside.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.900
If you ever need anything,
ask Shirou in here.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:24.860
What?

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.360
Hey!

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:31.990
Kuro.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.670
We're leaving early tomorrow.
Get to sleep.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:44.550
I know Shirou seems cold,
but he's a nice person.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.510
So his name is Shirou.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.050
What? He didn't tell you?

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.720
That's Shirou Ogami.
He's our social worker.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.980
Tomorrow, Shirou will be taking you
to the city hall.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.190
Ogami...

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.480
We don't have a bathtub,
but you want to take a shower, right?

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.400
Yes!

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.580
It's way different than I expected.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.840
It's packed!

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.220
See you later.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.680
What? You're leaving?

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:33.050
I only brought you
because I've got business here too.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.890
Take care of it yourself.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.350
Out of the way!

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.810
I'm in a hurry!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.940
I arrived before you!

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.400
What? Who do you think you are?

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:48.690
What's going on?

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.660
The young ones like
to show off their strength.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.910
That's not what I mean.
Aren't there any rules here?

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.330
There sure are.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.630
The strong ones win.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.460
It's a simple rule.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:11.340
What? You've got to be kidding.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.590
Get in line, or you'll never finish.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.980
I never thought
this city would be like this.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.610
That guy looks familiar.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.240
That could be the guy.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:35.370
Thank you for capturing the bombers.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:40.370
They were terrorists who'd been hired
by an anti-beastman organization.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.580
For money,
they'd even attack other beastmen.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:44.830
Very disappointing.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.880
Those scum are a disgrace
to all beastmen.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:52.720
By the way,
I have another favor to ask you.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:00.520
I knew it!

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.560
Cut that out!

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.730
-Give me back my wallet!
-I have never seen it!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.780
You darn well have!
You stole it from me yesterday!

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:17.120
-That's ancient history!
-It's not ancient! It was only yesterday!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.620
In this city, it's pointless
to worry about what happened yesterday.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.540
Have we met before?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.000
-You're that weasel!
-Mink!

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.010
I'm no weasel. I'm Marie the mink.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.600
You tanuki are such dopes! Goodbye!

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.430
I knew you were in cahoots!

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:43.270
I bet you were keeping watch!

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.480
You're in cahoots,
so you came to save him!

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.150
Oh, come now. It was a mere coincidence.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:49.940
It's a small city after all.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.110
Why don't you trust me?

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:56.530
Who do you have to thank
for getting you into this city anyway?

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.910
I paid you for it!

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.410
Gosh, fine.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:05.160
In this business, trust is everything,
so here's some free advice.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:08.330
Anything missing will turn up
in Rabbit Town.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.710
They all end up there.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:11.340
Rabbit Town?

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:15.380
That's right.
Pay Grand Grandma a visit there.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.520
There's not much of a bunny feel
to this place.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:27.980
Who the hell are you?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:32.690
You wouldn't happen to know
where I could find Grand Grandma, do you?

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:44.950
You've got guts coming here all morphed.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.710
Don't play dumb.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.420
Between gangs,
morphing means you're ready to rumble.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.510
Coming in here already morphed means
you're here for a fight!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:59.340
You've got me all wrong!
I can't control this myself!

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.220
I can't switch back from this form.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.310
You can't switch back?

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.060
You're not some baby!

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.680
Are you shitting me?

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.270
I shit you not! I really can't!

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.190
Until last year, I was a human.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.650
You were a human, you say?

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:19.530
Do you think we'd fall
for a bullshit excuse like that?

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.240
I can prove it!

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.540
My student ID is in my wallet
that got stolen yesterday.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.000
I came looking for that.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.960
Why did you think it would be here?

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:30.250
The weasel...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.460
I mean, Ms. Itami told me
you might know about it.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.880
Marie?

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.340
That's it! That's my wallet!

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:41.390
Look at my student ID in there!

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:43.640
-You'll see I'm--
-You're a student?

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.680
She's asking if you're a student!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.600
Yes, I am.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:52.860
If you are,
then you can read and write, right?

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.320
Yes, I can.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:59.280
I'll give you this back,
but on one condition.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.740
Will you do something for me?

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.160
Teach these kids how to read and write.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.790
What are kids doing here?

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:12.500
We who've been betrayed by men

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.500
end up here in Rabbit Town.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:19.760
For female beastmen
without anywhere to go,

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.140
we've got no choice
but to live relatively dangerous lives.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:28.060
These kids also know the pain
of being beastmen well.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:32.940
If they can at least read and write,
they might have a brighter future.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:36.770
If you do this,
you can have your wallet back.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.280
Fine! I'll do it!

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:41.490
MICHIRU

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.070
Who can read this?

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:47.030
Maybe one of you can?

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:50.660
Yes? You!

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.500
Poop!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.960
Well, that's not quite right.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.380
This is "Michiru."

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:01.720
It says "Michiru." That's my name.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.680
Okay, can anyone here write their name?

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:08.970
What's your name?

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:10.430
Youta.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.270
Youta, is it?

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.400
This is "Youta."

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:21.860
Youta. Try writing it.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.280
YOUTA

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:32.910
That's the way! That says "Youta."
That's your name.

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:38.790
Who else wants to learn
to write their name?

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:14.250
This place stinks of bitches as always.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:26.380
First, we'll memorize
all the hiragana characters.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:27.470
Are you listening?

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:32.310
You're good! Is that a wolf?

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.430
No. This is Silver Wolf.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:36.060
Silver Wolf?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.230
No way, Michiru!
You don't even know who Silver Wolf is?

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:41.770
No, I don't.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.530
He's the god of beastmen.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:49.740
When beastmen are truly in trouble,
a silver wolf comes and saves them.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.950
That story has been passed down for ages.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.500
I wonder if that was him.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.380
Michiru, have you seen him?

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.790
No way! Really?

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.590
No. I didn't see him up close.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.130
What?

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:11.470
So, Kusakabe, what are you here for?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.930
For business, obviously.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:16.640
Who would come here
if it weren't for work?

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.310
You call that work?

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.850
You're just here for the money.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.320
I told you, we don't have any money yet.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:26.990
"We don't have any!"
You think that's an excuse?

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:29.280
If you don't have any, then make some!

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:30.660
You should remember

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:35.240
who it is that's letting you women
make a living as gangsters!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.540
-Who cares, punk?
-Bring it on!

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.210
Lay off, Kusakabe.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:43.670
Boss?

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.760
I don't want to pick a fight
with you women either.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.630
Pay what you can, and we'll be on our way.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:55.640
It's not often
that you come around yourself, Flip.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.190
I thought I should pay you a visit
sometimes, Grand Grandma.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.110
What a load of bullshit.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.900
Even if you show up,
I still can't give you what I don't have.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.030
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.860
I heard you've got some new stuff.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.830
Sell them off,
and they'll get you some money, right?

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:18.870
How did you know about them?

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:21.170
Did you think you could hide them?

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:24.590
The mayor has started
to take notice as well.

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.300
What did you say?

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:30.380
It's all women are good for anyway.
It's totally obvious.

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:33.220
Unless they're sold
before they're snatched away,

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.430
they won't be worth a dime.

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:37.510
Do you get the picture?

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:40.770
The only reason you've got anything
is thanks to us!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.570
What's going on here?
What are you doing with us?

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:52.780
We're sending you all on a little trip.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:56.160
Don't tell me you're selling us!

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:00.660
I would have gotten more
if they could read a bit better.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.420
But I had to sell them off
sooner than I wanted.

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.880
That's why you wanted me to teach them?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.420
They're your children, right?
You can't be serious!

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.010
I never said they were our kids.

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:16.350
Then who are these children?

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:21.390
On their way to Anima-City, they got
separated from their parents or they died.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:25.350
What? You can't be serious.

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:27.610
That's so cruel!

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:32.320
In order to live,
the weak trample the weaker.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.570
That's what life is like here.

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:40.240
Save us, Silver Wolf.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.500
Asking a god to save you won't help.
You have to rely on yourself!

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.250
Hold on, everyone!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:09.060
That tanuki girl sure is tenacious.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:11.820
Reel it up!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.910
-It's no good.
-No, it's not!

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.620
Look! We're closer to the cab!

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.000
Don't ever give up!

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:31.300
Even in this city,
nobody's going to help you!

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:34.550
You've got to reach out
with your own hands

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:38.970
and grab it for yourself!

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.520
Keep trying,
but you'll never reach from that far away.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:54.190
Her arms! They're stretching!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.450
I've grabbed onto something!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:59.700
Damn! My arms stretched! Freaky!

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:02.830
-You're amazing, lady!
-But those arms are freaky.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:06.370
Don't call them freaky!
Wait! I think I've grabbed onto a lever.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.540
Yes!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.460
Pull that lever!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:13.840
What the heck is going on?

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.210
This is ridiculous!

00:18:15.300 --> 00:18:18.550
Just keep on pulling!

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:32.520
Okay. Everyone, run!

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.730
Hold it right there!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.150
That's a pretty clever trick.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:41.660
As I thought,
you're no ordinary beastman.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.700
Run!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.040
Let go of me!

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.040
-Knock her out.
-You got it.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:02.890
Who the fuck are you?

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.430
Silver Wolf.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:13.360
I won't tolerate lowlifes
who sell beastmen to humans.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:15.320
Even if they're women.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.280
You've asked for it now!

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:29.620
I surrender. Be kind to the elderly.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:43.260
I see you've done
a great job again, Ogami.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:47.970
We were having trouble getting a handle on
the gang that's been trafficking beastmen.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:50.480
The mayor asked me to help.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.480
What about the children?

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:55.610
Who is she?

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.150
She's a newbie.
The Beast Co-op is looking after her.

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:02.910
That was a pretty harsh welcome
you got, wasn't it?

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:06.450
Don't worry.
We'll take care of the children.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:10.160
We've got a facility
that takes in orphans like them.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:18.630
What do you want?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:22.340
How dare you? How could you sell children?

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:27.100
Even though you're beastmen,
don't you have a human heart?

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:33.560
Now I get it.
You really aren't a beastman, are you?

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.230
What's that supposed to mean?

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.440
Just try and say that

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:41.360
after you learn how hard it is
to make it alone as a woman

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.440
in the beastman world.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.080
What were you doing there?

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.670
You saw me from that rooftop, didn't you?

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.340
Yes.

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:01.380
Why didn't you help us then?

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.300
You knew we were going to be sold, right?

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.430
I still didn't have proof then.

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:09.050
To arrest them,
I had to catch them in the act.

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.020
What if you hadn't made it in time?

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.770
What if the ship had sailed?

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.600
We could have been sold off!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.150
Didn't you give any thought to those kids?

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:20.860
I never make mistakes.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.940
I will protect women and child beastmen.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.700
Women and children?

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:29.530
What makes males so special?
Are men really that great?

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.080
Look at my ID and see that I'm a human!

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:35.160
SPECIES: HUMAN

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:38.130
How can you say you don't make mistakes?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.170
Can't you see you've made a mistake?

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.760
I hate this city
and all the beastmen in it!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:47.130
I'm going to get over this disease
and leave this city!

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:50.410
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
